From 0c6e002472ac1871f216535c297364f11c2f9bd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zenium Upstream Port <upstream-port@zenium.invalid>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 03:26:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 70/82] arm64: dts: mediatek: transplant the even board device
 tree

The device's DT surface is a base board file plus /plugin/ overlays, not a board file
authored against upstream bindings: even_defconfig appends `mediatek/mt6768` and
builds five overlays (oplus6768_20761, oplus6769_2167A, oplus6769_216AF,
oplus6769_226AF, oplus6769_226BE) whose board data covers touch IC, camera modules,
charger ICs (bq2589x/bq25910/rt9471/sy6974), battery tables and Type-C config.

`upstream-port/bin/dtsport.py` computes the include closure with kbuild's own search
paths and transplants it: 55 files, of which 49 do not exist in 5.15 at all (copied),
6 collide with mainline files, and 7 are dt-binding headers the target lacks
(mt6768-clk.h, mt6768-gce.h, mt6382-gce.h, mt6768-larb-port.h, mt6768-msdc.h,
mt6358-irq.h, mediatek,boot-mode.h, mt635x-auxadc.h). Vendor-only board directories
(arch/arm64/boot/dts/oplus6769_*/cust.dtsi) keep their 4.19 layout so the overlays'
relative includes still resolve.

One collision needed a real decision. `mediatek/mt6358.dtsi` exists in mainline 5.15
too, but with different contents: the vendor copy defines the PMIC regulator/interrupt
labels this board references by phandle (`mt_pmic_vmodem_buck_reg`,
`mt_pmic_vmc_ldo_reg`, `mt6358_vmch_eint_low`, ...). Keeping mainline's file aborts
`make dtbs` with dtc `ERROR (phandle_references)`; overwriting it silently changes
mt8183-evb/kukui/pumpkin, which include the same path. So the vendor file is installed
as a device-private shadow copy, `mt6358-mt6768.dtsi`, and the board's #include is
pointed at it - other boards keep mainline's, this board gets the labels it needs.
Generic dt-binding headers (gpio.h, irq.h, arm-gic.h, phy.h, mt65xx.h) are
deliberately *not* shadowed: those are pure constants and 5.15's drivers are written
against 5.15's revision of them.

Verified on 5.15: mt6768.dtb 122,474 bytes (629 nodes, 2,538 properties, 413
compatible properties), and all five overlays as .dtbo, each round-trip clean through
dtc. The overlays carry __fixups__/__local_fixups__ (no __symbols__: kbuild's cmd_dtc
builds them without -@, which is correct for one-overlay-on-base merging, not for
chained overlays).
